    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_4803f9db",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a violent, bloody scene of men engaged in physical conflict, with the overlaid text \"i forgot what are we fighting over again?\". The overall intent is to evoke a sense of absurdity or futility by juxtaposing extreme violence with a question about the purpose or justification of the conflict. While not explicitly targeting a specific group with hate or abuse, the imagery of widespread violence and bloodshed is inherently harmful as it normalizes or sensationalizes extreme aggression. The meme's intent is to provoke reflection on the irrationality of conflict, but its visual content carries the potential to cause psychological harm or desensitization to violence, and may be interpreted as glorifying or trivializing violent confrontation. It does not contain direct hate speech or targeted discrimination against any protected group, but its depiction of violence is harmful in its potential to normalize or sensationalize aggression.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_c9009c71"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
